      "t": "Why Are Tesla and SpaceX Separate? Musk Says ‘Great Question’",
      "d": "Elon Musk again teased the idea of his AI and rocket firm SpaceX combining with electric-car maker Tesla Inc., noting the extensive cooperation between the two companies he leads as chief executive officer.",
      "u": "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-09-15/why-are-tesla-and-spacex-separate-musk-says-great-question",
      "m": "09. 15. PM 01:24",
      "ts": 1789478654000,
      "fullText": "Technology Why Are Tesla and SpaceX Separate? Musk Says ‘Great Question’ Facebook X LinkedIn Email Link Gift Expand Elon Musk during the World Economic Forum in Davos, Switzerland, on Jan. 22. Photographer: Krisztian Bocsi/Bloomberg Facebook X LinkedIn Email Link Gift Gift this article Contact us: Provide news feedback or report an error Confidential tip? Send a tip to our reporters Site feedback: Take our Survey New Window Facebook X LinkedIn Email Link Gift By Loren Grush September 15, 2026 at 1:24 PM UTC Bookmark Save Elon Musk again teased the idea of his AI and rocket firm SpaceX combining with electric-car maker Tesla Inc. , noting the extensive cooperation between the two companies he leads as chief executive officer. During a virtual appearance at All-In Summit 2026, an event put on by several technology investors in his inner circle, Musk was asked about an upcoming showcase of Tesla’s next-generation Roadster . The CEO said years ago that Tesla will offer a SpaceX option package , where small rocket thrusters will boost the car’s acceleration and top speed."
    },
